Whether you will deploy resources in the same Region or AZ for Blue-Green, how would your Application deployed in Blue switch to Green, How the Synchronisation would happen, Including Intricacies of Routing within the Switching Process ?!


Blue-Green only works correctly when both environments run in the same Region/AZ.
Doing Blue-Green across Regions is not practical — network latency, DB consistency, and routing updates will break the switch. So cross-region Blue-Green is generally NOT done.

The switch from Blue → Green is simple:
the Load Balancer/Ingress just changes the target from Blue to Green once Green is healthy.
That’s the only “switching mechanism.” No special sync happens between Blue and Green.

Both environments use the same database.
As long as the schema is backward-compatible, the app can switch instantly without any data issues.
That’s why the process works only when everything is in the same Region/AZ and sharing the same backend.
